{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477671-disciplines-whilst-in-torpor-rev","id":1477671,"title":"Disciplines whilst in torpor (Rev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-30T02:26:31-07:00","id":1477671,"title":"Disciplines whilst in torpor (Rev)","content":"Greetings all,<br /> <br /> Unless I'm seriously overlooking it, it's not clear to me which powers can be used whilst in torpor.<br /> It's clear that no blood can be spent and only mental disciplines apply.<br /> <br /> Specifically allowed are:<br /> <br /> Auspex 6: The dreaming<br /> Auspex 9: False slumber<br /> Dominate 7: Strings of the marionette<br /> <br /> What about Presence, Dementation, Obfuscate?<br /> (any power that does not require blood spent and no physical interaction)<br /> <br /> Are they by default not allowed because it's not specifically mentioned?<br /> ST's decision?<br /> <br /> Also can you spend willpower?<br /> <br /> Apologies if this has been discussed or if I missed the rules, but I'm not finding it.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T05:58:26-07:00","id":1477682,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to go beyond revised, there is Pulse of the City in the V20 core (and in revised's Guide to the Camarilla), and A Perfect World in Guide to the High Clans (DAV). Both are Presence 9 powers. Pulse of the City requires expenditure of willpower to enact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":699,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","user":"MalleusXXIII","date":". 03-30-2022, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T08:19:32-07:00","id":1477685,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure at least certain levels of animalism could be. I also think summon can be used. I think there are several powers which could theoretically be used, but they have conditions which couldn't practically be met, such as dominate requiring eye contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}